OL,3,GNEWSAStranger to row Atlantic with crew
OL,4,Ain ocean dash
OL,5,
OL,6,FA stranger, found on social media after
OL,7,Fan appeal, will join three gig rowers
OL,8,Fon a grueling journey across the
OL,9,FAtlantic.
OL,11,FThe crew, from Cornwall and Dorset,
OL,12,Fwill be attempting the 3,200 mile
OL,13,F(5,149km) row unsupported as part of
OL,14,Fthe Atlantic Dash event in January.
OL,16,FWith their fourth and final crew
OL,17,Fmember, who was from Devon, forced to
OL,18,Fwithdraw due to sea sickness, the team
OL,19,Fturned to social media for a solution.
OL,23,APub: 25-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,344,340,200,160,0,100
